index.description=Algorab is a programming language designed to meet the educational needs on high and higher education for teaching programming and algorithms. Inspired by the research of the last few decades, Algorab promotes effective learning of algorithms and good programming practices.
index.quickstart.title=Quick to get started
index.quickstart.text=Algorab allows students to start practising quickly by being easy to install on all platforms and simple to use thanks to its low-ceremony syntax, allowing teachers to save time on the first lessons.
index.expressivity.title=Expressive
index.expressivity.text=Most algorithms and data structures are tedious to write in languages such as Python, C or Java, while not being easy to reread. Algorab imports concepts from functional programming such as algebraic data types and pattern matching to make classic algorithmic problems clear and concise to describe.
index.assistance.title=Active assistance for students in their learning
index.assistance.text=Most programming languages do not provide the necessary tools for beginners to understand the issues they encounter, resulting in dropouts and times losses. Algorab has clear and precise error messages to help students understand and solve problems on their own.
index.professionalisation.title=Industry-relevant skills
index.professionalisation.text=Algorab encourages the use of good programming practices such as error handling, correct naming, adding comments and writing tests. With Algorab, students acquire skills that can be applied to the languages used in the professional world.
index.opensource.title=Free as in freedom
index.opensource.text=While some companies focus on maximising profitability, we have chosen to have a social impact. We are concerned about education and scientific research. Algorab is licensed under a free software licence, allowing anyone to use, study, modify and redistribute the project, promoting knowledge sharing and collaboration a sustainable future.
index.indev.title=Project in development
index.indev.text=Algorab is still in development. The website will be edited as the project progresses and news will be sent to newsletter subscribers.
